  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 805-20-25-10, identifiable intangible assets acquired in a business combination must be recognized separately from goodwill at their acquisition-date fair values. An intangible qualifies if it meets the contractual-legal criterion or the separability criterion. All four items here satisfy at least one criterion.
Wrong (A): Lumping intangibles into goodwill violates ASC 805, which requires separate recognition of identifiable intangible assets distinct from goodwill.
Wrong (B): ASC 805 recognizes intangibles meeting either the contractual-legal or the separability criterion—not just the contractual-legal criterion alone.
Wrong (C): The acquiree''s historical cost is irrelevant; acquired intangibles are recorded at acquisition-date fair value regardless of whether the acquiree carried them on its books.$EXPL$
