-- Q4850: Foreign Currency Transactions [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 830-30-45-12, translation adjustments from the current rate method are reported in other comprehensive income and accumulate in AOCI within stockholders'' equity. The CTA is not recognized in net income until sale or substantial liquidation of the foreign investment.
Wrong (A): Translation adjustments bypass the income statement entirely; only remeasurement gains and losses under the temporal method are reported in net income.
Wrong (B): The CTA is not posted directly to retained earnings; it is a separate component of comprehensive income accumulated in AOCI.
Wrong (C): The translation reserve is not outside equity—AOCI is a component within stockholders'' equity on the balance sheet.$EXPL$
