-- Q4851: Foreign Currency Transactions [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 830-10-45-17, the temporal method remeasures monetary items (cash, receivables, payables) at the current exchange rate. These items represent fixed claims denominated in foreign currency and must reflect the balance sheet date rate.
Wrong (A): Inventory carried at cost is a nonmonetary asset remeasured at the historical exchange rate under the temporal method, not the current rate.
Wrong (B): PP&E is a nonmonetary asset carried at historical cost and is remeasured at the historical exchange rate, not the current rate.
Wrong (D): Prepaid expenses are nonmonetary items remeasured at historical rates under the temporal method because they represent advance payments, not monetary claims.$EXPL$
